    "role": "assistant",
    "type": "assistant_message",
    "content": "All 22 checklist items have been tested and recorded — the run is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**18 PASS / 4 FAIL**\n\nThe core browsing, searching, filtering, sorting, detail-page, and admin CRUD flows all work well. Four defects were found:\n\n**FT-19 — No data persistence (most severe).** All product data lives in memory only. Creating \"QA Minimal Product\" succeeded, but after a page reload it was gone and only the 9 seeded products remained. `localStorage`/`sessionStorage` are empty and there is no backend API, so every admin edit is lost the moment the page reloads.\n\n**CS-20 — Incomplete publish validation.** Only name, category and short description are enforced. A product was published with no full review, no image, no retailer link and zero specifications. Price also accepts negative values — a product saved with price `-50` renders as `-$50`. Only the rating field is properly bounded (0–5).\n\n**FT-4 — Tag filter list is hardcoded.** New tags saved on products (e.g. `qa-percussion` on Theragun Pro) appear on the detail page and in keyword search, but never become filter choices — the Filters panel always shows the same 35 seeded tags. Removed tags (`massage`, `therapy`) also linger as stale, now-unmatched options.\n\n**FT-2 — Featured set can't be fully browsed.** Toggling featured does update the homepage strip, but that strip is capped at 3, so with 4 featured products the newly featured one was silently omitted. Its \"View all\" link points to `/products?featured=true`, and that page ignores the parameter entirely — it returned all 10 products.\n\nOne minor observation not covered by a checklist item: the price range control renders a single thumb labelled \"Minimum\" that actually drives the *maximum* price, and its `aria-valuenow` stays at 0 while the displayed max changes. It also doesn't respond to keyboard input (End/Arrow keys), so the filter is mouse-drag-only — an accessibility gap."
  }
}
